\title{pSI: Specificity Index Statistic}
\description{
Tools for the Specificity Index (pSI) statistic, which identifies genes
enriched in specific cell types or tissues from a matrix of expression
profiles, and for Cell type-Specific Expression Analysis (CSEA) of candidate
gene lists. The typical workflow is:
\enumerate{
  \item \code{\link{specificity.index}} computes pSI values from an expression
    matrix with genes in rows and cell types/samples in columns.
  \item \code{\link{pSI.list}} and \code{\link{pSI.count}} list and count the
    genes specific to each cell type at four pSI thresholds
    (0.05, 0.01, 0.001, 0.0001).
  \item \code{\link{candidate.overlap}} and \code{\link{fisher.iteration}}
    intersect a candidate gene list with those specific genes and test the
    overlap for significance with Fisher's exact test.
}
Bundled example data: \code{\link{sample.data}}, \code{\link{candidate.genes}}
and \code{\link{dataset.s1}}.
}
\section{Supplementary data}{

Precomputed pSI tables for mouse cell types (bacTRAP) and human brain regions
(BrainSpan), formerly distributed as the companion package \code{pSI.data}
from a lab web page that no longer exists, are hosted separately because they
are too large for CRAN. See the package README for the current download
location.
}

